      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">AccuWeb VPS Review 2026: Managed KVM from $4.95/mo, 16 Global DCs</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-base">Last updated: August 27, 2026 · 9 min read</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-5">

      <p>Most of the budget VPS providers we cover sell stripped-down unmanaged KVM: you get root access, a panel, and not much else. AccuWeb Hosting takes a different lane. Founded in 2003 with a 23+ year operating history, AccuWeb sells Linux and Windows VPS on KVM and Xen virtualization with <strong>dedicated vCPUs (no overselling)</strong>, ECC RAM, enterprise pure-SSD storage on RAID 6 / RAID 10, and SOC 2 Type II certified data centers across 16+ global locations — while promo pricing starts at just <strong>$4.95/month</strong>. We pulled the live plan data from the official accuwebhosting.com VPS pages in August 2026, verified the company background, and stacked the lineup against the budget anchors we already cover.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">AccuWeb at a Glance</h2>
      <p>AccuWeb Hosting was founded in <strong>2003</strong> and is part of the <strong>Vaghasia Group of Companies</strong>; the company reports servicing over <strong>55,000 web hosting accounts</strong> across shared, VPS, cloud, and dedicated hosting on both Linux and Windows. The footer carries "Copyright © 2003-2026" and the about page states "23+ years of experience." This is a materially different profile from the young budget hosts (VirMach, DediRock, HostNOC) that often top the low-end discussion — AccuWeb is a mid-market infrastructure provider that happens to run aggressive entry promos. We verified the Linux VPS product page, the plan JSON (1, 2, 3, and 4-vCPU tiers at $4.95-$19.95/mo promo), the technical specifications grid, and the data-center list directly from the official site in August 2026.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">The Linux VPS line — 4 core tiers, $4.95 to $19.95/month (promo)</h2>
      <p>The headline Linux VPS product is a clean 4-tier lineup: 1 to 4 dedicated vCPUs, 4 to 32 GB RAM, 50 to 400 GB of pure SSD storage, and 250 GB to 1 TB of transfer on a 1 Gbps port. Every plan ships with a dedicated IP, full root access, a choice of OS templates, and optional managed service. The four verified promo tiers are:</p>

